spec ab04-retry-loop-converges: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# AB04. WW03's two increments of x.v, each run by a client that retries the whole
# transaction on a retriable refusal (a serialization conflict, or the poisoning it
# leaves), up to three attempts. The final x.v must equal the number of increments
# acknowledged, in every interleaving: a retry never double-applies and an
# acknowledged increment is never lost.

starting permutation: s1go s1fin s2go s2fin
step s1go: <retrier: BEGIN; SET x.v = x.v + 1>
step s1fin: <retrier: COMMIT, retry on a retriable refusal>
attempts|acknowledged
--------+------------
1       |true        
(1 row)
step s2go: <retrier: BEGIN; SET x.v = x.v + 1>
step s2fin: <retrier: COMMIT, retry on a retriable refusal>
attempts|acknowledged
--------+------------
1       |true        
(1 row)
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'x'}) RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
2
(1 row)

